[217.689156, "o", "\t-T                                   : \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ktest\u001b[m\u001b[K configuration file (use with -c)\r\n\t--list-keywords[=all|csv|<kword>]    : list keywords implemented by the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kengine\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\t--runmode <runmode_id>               : specific runmode modification the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kengine\u001b[m\u001b[K should run.  The argument\r\n\t--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kengine\u001b[m\u001b[K-analysis                    : print reports on analysis of different sections in the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kengine\u001b[m\u001b[K and exit.\r\n\t                                       Please have a look at the conf parameter \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kengine\u001b[m\u001b[K-analysis on what reports\r\n\t--disable-detection                  : disable detection \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kengine\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\t--simulate-ips                       : force \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kengine\u001b[m\u001b[K into IPS mode. Useful for QA\r\nTo run the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kengine\u001b[m\u001b[K with default configuration on interface eth0 with signature file \"signatures.\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krule\u001b[m\u001b[Ks\", run the command as:\r\nsuricata -c suricata.yaml -s signatures.\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krule\u001b[m\u001b[Ks -i eth0 \r\n"]
